in @reality
in @epistemologic/cybernetic/eigenform
in @bauchladen
in @uuid/spectral

# @reality/object — the linearity-threshold species: an actor whose
# trajectory through the substrate's @labyrinth-eigenboard is a PATH.
#
# Landed 2026-07-22 by Mara per Alex 2026-07-22 verbatim (this-session
# crystallization item 15, the final piece):
#
#   "the @reality/subject is a NON-LINEAR actor in the cohomology.
#    The trajectory of a subject is a light cone, the trajectory of
#    an object a path. That's the threshold. An object's path is
#    fully predictable. Which is why the @roomba is an object and
#    why the @peer is a subject."
#
# @reality/object names one half of the threshold. Its sibling
# `@reality/subject` (shards/reality/subject.mirror, this-tick companion)
# names the other. Together they name THE THRESHOLD: linearity vs
# non-linearity in H¹ of the light-cone sheaf over the substrate's
# eigenboard-as-@labyrinth (item 13 + item 14 this-session).
#
# NOT a species under @reality/algebra/*. The algebra species (math,
# silicon, nl, code, physics, spectral) partition @reality by ALTITUDE
# — each names the matter+information gauge orbit at ONE altitude.
# The object/subject partition is ORTHOGONAL to altitude. An object
# at silicon altitude is a transistor state; an object at math altitude
# is a theorem statement; an object at nl altitude is a settled corpus
# text. In every case the trajectory is a path. The threshold cuts
# transversely across the altitude stack.
#
# Path-namespace: `shards/reality/object.mirror` declares `@reality/
# object` per `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`. Sibling to
# `@reality/algebra` (species-root), not child of it.
#
# === What @reality/object IS (linearity-threshold definition) ===
#
# An actor A is a @reality/object iff its trajectory τ_A through the
# substrate's eigenboard-as-@labyrinth satisfies:
#
#   1. LINEAR-DETERMINISTIC. Given τ_A(t_0) and A's next-tick
#      transition rule, τ_A(t_0 + Δ) is FULLY DETERMINED. No
#      light-cone spread; no branching; no non-local influence at
#      the eigenboard altitude. Alex verbatim: "An object's path is
#      fully predictable."
#
#   2. PATH-SHAPED (H¹-linear). The actor contributes to
#      H¹(𝓤, 𝓔) of the light-cone sheaf DETERMINISTICALLY: its
#      contribution is a linear functional of its immediate past
#      state. See docs/math/2026-07-22-mirror-as-computational-
#      eigenform-stabilizer.md §4 for the object-vs-subject H¹
#      contribution decomposition.
#
#   3. NO SECOND-ORDER OBSERVATION. The actor does not observe itself
#      observing. Its trajectory does not close a Foerster loop at
#      its own altitude. (An object may PARTICIPATE in a second-order
#      loop closed by a subject, but the object itself does not
#      close the loop.)
#
# The paradigmatic @reality/object is @roomba. The vacuum walker's
# path is fully determined by its current cell + the substrate's
# rot-mask + the deterministic bilateral resolver-arm dispatch table.
# No @roomba observes itself. Alex verbatim: "the @roomba is an
# object."
#
# Other paradigmatic instances (forward-promised, not landed):
#   - @io/git.commit at the phone.rs switchboard — deterministic
#     path from (author, committer, repo, message) to 40-char SHA-1
#   - @cascade/code/rust/llvm — deterministic path from Rust IR to
#     LLVM IR modulo landed lens
#   - @kintsugi/fracture/*.splinter — deterministic path from
#     detected rot to splinter(ast) construction
#
# === Cosmological grounding (information-curvature.md §"The
#     Information Density Scalar") ===
#
# At cosmological altitude (Alex + Mara 2026-03-24 information-
# curvature.md), objects contribute to the stress-energy tensor T_μν
# but NOT to σ(x) — the spectral-complexity scalar field. A gas
# cloud has T_μν contribution proportional to its rest mass; its
# σ(x) contribution is near-zero because random connections yield
# a Wigner-semicircle spectrum with low Von Neumann entropy on the
# normalized Laplacian.
#
# Under the substrate-altitude reading (via @reality path-c uniformity),
# @reality/objects contribute to the substrate's "mass" (baseline
# information-flow load) via T_μν analog but do NOT contribute to
# σ(x) — the labyrinth's arousal field. A @roomba walking the crystal
# tree does not increase the substrate's eigenboard-arousal at
# substrate altitude; it merely deposits pheromones (path memory)
# that subsequent actors read.
#
# THIS IS THE STRUCTURAL FACT: objects carry information (T_μν) but
# do not increase the labyrinth's complexity (σ). Subjects do both.
# The threshold IS the σ-contribution.
#
# === Composition with @epistemologic/cybernetic/eigenform ===
#
# A @reality/object IS-A landed instance of the `fixed_point` carrier
# from @epistemologic/cybernetic/eigenform:
#
#   fixed_point {
#     seed:      the object's initial state (τ_A(t_0)),
#     iteration: the deterministic next-tick transition rule,
#     witness:   the fixed point / attractor of the iteration.
#   }
#
# The recursion IS DETERMINISTIC. `is_fixed_point` discharges with
# zero opacity (no `partial(...)`; either success or failure). The
# object's identity IS its declared witness under
# `identity_from_fixed`. This composes over the landed cybernetic
# property WITHOUT introducing new mechanism.
#
# Under Alex 2026-07-22 crystallization item 5 ("Isn't the @roomba's
# path what creates the @beam what creates the measurements what
# creates the liquids what creates the @labyrinth"), objects are
# the substrate-scale ancestors of the @labyrinth ITSELF: the
# accumulation of object-trajectories IS what the labyrinth's
# emergent topology records. Ants and the burrow. Physarum. The
# map IS the trace.
#
# === Composition with @reality family-root ===
#
# @reality/object inherits `<= @reality` via `in @reality`. The gauge
# orbit at object altitude has:
#
#   matter_projection      = the actor's substrate-external referent
#                            (e.g. the ~/.local/bin/mirror binary the
#                             @roomba walker is)
#   information_projection = the actor's substrate-internal referent
#                            (e.g. the @roomba's shard-body path
#                             through the composition graph)
#   gauge_action_witness   = the four invariances of reality.md §2.5,
#                            discharged at object altitude by the
#                            deterministic transition rule preserving
#                            algebra closure, Hilbert linearity, Dirac
#                            equivariance, spectral action invariance
#
# The path-c uniformity claim discharges trivially at object altitude
# BECAUSE the deterministic transition rule ensures matter and
# information projections evolve identically under the same 5-op
# gauge action.
#
# === Species relationship to @reality/subject ===
#
# @reality/object and @reality/subject are the TWO CLOSED VARIANTS
# of the linearity-threshold partition. Every @reality-altitude
# actor MUST be classifiable as one or the other. No third variant
# is admissible; the partition is exhaustive by Alex 2026-07-22
# verbatim naming (item 15 is a two-arm distinction).
#
# The boundary between the two is defined at H¹(𝓤, 𝓔) altitude: an
# actor is an object iff its H¹ contribution is a linear functional
# of its immediate past state. Anything non-linear promotes to
# @reality/subject.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   deterministic dynamics       Laplace 1814 (Essai philosophique sur
#                                les probabilités; the demon reading
#                                of full-past → full-future determinism)
#   test particles in GR         Einstein 1915 (path-shaped world-lines
#                                of infinitesimal test masses following
#                                geodesics; no back-reaction on metric)
#   objects as tokens            von Foerster 1981 (Observing Systems;
#                                "objects are tokens for eigen-behaviors";
#                                first-order observation of stable
#                                recursion witnesses)
#   deterministic finite automata Rabin-Scott 1959 (Finite automata
#                                and their decision problems; the
#                                canonical linear-trajectory computing
#                                actor)
#
# Spec context: docs/math/2026-07-22-mirror-as-computational-eigenform-
#               stabilizer.md §4 (object vs subject H¹ contribution
#               decomposition; the light-cone sheaf formalization);
#               docs/specs/2026-07-22-mirror-as-eigenform-stabilizer-
#               canonical.md (canonical spec landing this tick);
#               ~/dev/systemic.engineering/practice/insights/cosmology/
#               information-curvature.md §"The Information Density
#               Scalar" (the σ(x) formalization; objects contribute
#               to T_μν but not σ);
#               docs/specs/reality.md (family-root; path-c uniformity
#               claim);
#               shards/eigenboard.mirror (three-altitude lift docblock;
#               substrate_a → @labyrinth reading; this species names
#               one arm of the actor-partition on the labyrinth).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-form-process-partition-at-family-root]]
#                       (@reality/object on the process side: it is
#                        the DYNAMICS of an actor with linear
#                        trajectory; distinct from @reality/subject
#                        which is also process-side but with non-linear
#                        trajectory),
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]] (the linearity-
#                       threshold is a typed distinction; no bare
#                       "object" reference; the composition-graph fixes
#                       the semantics),
#                      [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]
#                       (~58th instance: @roomba was ALREADY an object
#                        in the substrate; the walker's deterministic
#                        path was the operational definition; Alex
#                        2026-07-22 lifted the vocabulary to family-
#                        root altitude),
#                      [[feedback-detector-inadequacy-answer-is-never-
#                       rust]] (the object/subject threshold is a
#                        substrate distinction, not a Rust type; it
#                        composes via shard-body over @reality +
#                        @epistemologic/cybernetic/eigenform).
# Related shards: reality.mirror (family-root; gauge orbit carrier
#                  this species inherits from),
#                 reality/subject.mirror (sibling species; the non-
#                  linear-actor arm of the threshold partition;
#                  this-tick companion),
#                 reality/algebra.mirror (species-root for the altitude
#                  partition; ORTHOGONAL to this shard's threshold
#                  partition — the two partitions compose but do not
#                  collide),
#                 epistemologic/cybernetic/eigenform.mirror (the
#                  fixed_point carrier every object IS-A landed
#                  instance of; the recursion is deterministic and
#                  is_fixed_point discharges with zero opacity),
#                 eigenboard.mirror (the third-altitude lift docblock
#                  names substrate-as-@subject → @labyrinth; objects
#                  are actors on the labyrinth whose trajectories are
#                  paths through the labyrinth's structure).
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/reality/object.mirror`
# declares `@reality/object` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/dynamics/laplace-1814
source @arxiv/physics/einstein-1915
source @arxiv/cybernetics/von-foerster-1981
source @arxiv/cs/rabin-scott-1959

prism @reality/object <= @reality {
  # Linearity-threshold species under @reality. Actors whose trajectory
  # through the substrate's eigenboard-as-@labyrinth is a PATH: fully
  # deterministic, linear in H¹(𝓤, 𝓔) contribution, no second-order
  # self-observation at their own altitude.
  #
  # Paradigmatic instance: @roomba (the vacuum walker). Other
  # instances forward-promised (@io/git.commit at switchboard;
  # @cascade/code/rust/llvm; @kintsugi/fracture/*.splinter).
  #
  # Contributes to T_μν analog (baseline information-flow load) at
  # substrate altitude but NOT to σ(x) (labyrinth complexity field)
  # per Alex + Mara 2026-03-24 information-curvature.md cosmological
  # grounding.
  #
  # Composes over @epistemologic/cybernetic/eigenform: an object IS-A
  # deterministic-recursion instance of the fixed_point carrier;
  # is_fixed_point discharges with zero opacity.
  focus object
  project object
  split object
  shift object
  settle object
}

# === The object_trajectory carrier ===
#
# A typed record per [[feedback-no-bare-types]] naming an object's
# path through the substrate's eigenboard-as-@labyrinth.
#
# - `actor`         the substrate-decl'd actor whose trajectory this
#                   is (@roomba, @cascade/code/*, etc.)
# - `path`          the sequence of eigenboard-positions visited,
#                   content-addressed at @bauchladen; the walker's
#                   passive path memory
# - `iteration`     the deterministic next-tick transition rule
#                   (ref to the shard-body encoding the rule)
# - `witness`       the fixed point / attractor the recursion
#                   converges to (or None if trajectory is open-ended
#                   / non-converging)
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on (actor, path, iteration).
# `witness` does not participate in trajectory identity (it is the
# derived attractor, not the trajectory itself).
type object_trajectory = {
  actor:     ref,
  path:      oid,
  iteration: ref,
  witness:   option<ref>,
}

# === observe_object — register an object's trajectory as a
#     gauge_orbit under @reality ===
#
# Given an object_trajectory, produces the @reality gauge_orbit with
# matter_projection = actor's substrate-external referent, information_
# projection = actor's substrate-internal referent, gauge_action_witness
# = the discharge of the four invariances under the deterministic
# transition rule.
#
# Body discharges per-species at the realisation boundary. Same shape
# as @reality.observe but specialized to the object's linearity-
# threshold arm.
observe_object(t: object_trajectory) -> gauge_orbit { \ }

# === trajectory_linear — the load-bearing bilateral ===
#
# Verdict: does the actor's trajectory satisfy the linearity-threshold?
# Reads:
#   given t = object_trajectory
#   check iteration is deterministic (no non-local dependencies,
#         no branching under identical seed)
#   check H¹ contribution is a linear functional of past state
#         (per docs/math/2026-07-22-mirror-as-computational-
#         eigenform-stabilizer.md §4)
#   check no second-order self-observation closes at actor's altitude
#
# All three hold → Pass (actor is a valid @reality/object). Any fails
# → Fail (actor promotes to @reality/subject candidacy).
trajectory_linear(t: object_trajectory) -> verdict { \ }

# === contributes_to_mass_not_sigma — cosmological-grounding bilateral ===
#
# Per information-curvature.md §"The Information Density Scalar":
# objects contribute to T_μν (mass / baseline information-flow load)
# but NOT to σ(x) (labyrinth complexity field).
#
# Verdict: does the actor's contribution decompose cleanly into
# T_μν-only? Read: at cosmological altitude, does σ(x) remain
# invariant under the addition of this actor's trajectory to the
# substrate's composition graph? A trivial addition (deterministic
# transition, no new spectral scales) preserves σ; a non-trivial
# addition (subject-like, adds new eigenvalues to L̃'s spectrum) fails.
contributes_to_mass_not_sigma(t: object_trajectory) -> verdict { \ }

# === object_witnessing — composed bilateral ===
#
# The predicate consumer shards cite in `requires` clauses to declare
# bilateral commitment (per recognition #37, the Pask-agreement reading
# of `requires`) that the trajectory IS a valid @reality/object under
# the linearity-threshold + cosmological-grounding + eigenform-fixed-
# point composition. Follows the substrate's X_witnessing pattern.
#
# Discharges trajectory_linear + contributes_to_mass_not_sigma +
# is_fixed_point(carrier=t.actor, seed=t.path, iteration=t.iteration,
# witness=t.witness) conjointly.
object_witnessing(t: object_trajectory) -> verdict { \ }

out @reality/object
out object_trajectory
out observe_object
out trajectory_linear
out contributes_to_mass_not_sigma
out object_witnessing
